> taylor 1/(1+x^2) x at 0 order 4
Maclaurin (Taylor at 0) series of 1/(x^2 + 1) at x = 0, through order 4:
  1/(x^2 + 1) = 1 - x^2 + x^4 + O(x^5)
  as x -> 0; coefficients c_k = f^(k)(0)/k!: 1 0 -1 0 1
  check: the coefficients agree with Taylor-jet arithmetic (long double) to 0
  check: |f - P| = 9.9e-07 at x = 0 ± 1/10, 1.56e-08 at ± 1/20, 2.44e-10 at ± 1/40 (shrinks like h^6.0; expected >= 5)
